## Root cause analysis

I did a deep dive into the codebase and identified **3 code-level root causes** for this bug (confirmed on latest `origin/dev` at `cd8e8a9`). These affect OpenAI reasoning models (o3, o4-mini, GPT-5) on the Responses API path.

### Root Cause 1: `differentModel` strips `providerMetadata` (reasoningEncryptedContent / itemId)

**File:** `packages/opencode/src/session/message-v2.ts:669,754`

```typescript
const differentModel = `${model.providerID}/${model.id}` !== `${msg.info.providerID}/${msg.info.modelID}`
// ...
if (part.type === "reasoning") {
  assistantMessage.parts.push({
    type: "reasoning",
    text: part.text,
    ...(differentModel ? {} : { providerMetadata: part.metadata }),
  })
}
```

When the model changes between turns (even switching between variants of the same model), `providerMetadata` is completely dropped. This means `reasoningEncryptedContent` and `itemId` are lost. The downstream converter then has no reasoning data to pass back to the API.

### Root Cause 2: `convert-to-openai-responses-input.ts` skips reasoning when `itemId` is null

**File:** `packages/opencode/src/provider/sdk/copilot/responses/convert-to-openai-responses-input.ts:193,238-242`

```typescript
const reasoningId = providerOptions?.itemId
if (reasoningId != null) {
  // ... builds reasoning item
} else {
  warnings.push({
    type: "other",
    message: `Non-OpenAI reasoning parts are not supported. Skipping reasoning part: ${JSON.stringify(part)}.`,
  })
}
```

When `itemId` is null (which happens after Root Cause 1, or when using non-OpenAI providers), the reasoning part is **completely skipped** with only a warning. This is exactly what Vercel AI SDK fixed in [vercel/ai#12869](https://github.com/vercel/ai/pull/12869) — when `encrypted_content` is present, reasoning items should still be included even without `itemId`.

### Root Cause 3: `include: ["reasoning.encrypted_content"]` only set in variant options

**File:** `packages/opencode/src/provider/transform.ts:508-516`

```typescript
case "@ai-sdk/openai":
  return Object.fromEntries(
    openaiEfforts.map((effort) => [
      effort,
      {
        reasoningEffort: effort,
        reasoningSummary: "auto",
        include: ["reasoning.encrypted_content"],
      },
    ]),
  )
```

The `include: ["reasoning.encrypted_content"]` is only set inside `variants()` options. When no variant is explicitly selected (default model settings), `encrypted_content` is never requested from the API. Without it, there's nothing to pass back on subsequent turns.

### Related Vercel AI SDK fixes (for reference)

These are the same class of bugs that were fixed in the Vercel AI SDK:
- [vercel/ai#12869](https://github.com/vercel/ai/pull/12869) — include reasoning without `itemId` when `encrypted_content` is present
- [vercel/ai#14418](https://github.com/vercel/ai/pull/14418) — support encrypted reasoning round-trip for ZDR accounts

However, opencode has its own custom converter (`convert-to-openai-responses-input.ts`), so those SDK fixes don't automatically apply here.

### Suggested fix direction

1. In `message-v2.ts`: Even when `differentModel` is true, preserve `providerMetadata` for reasoning parts if the target model is also a reasoning model
2. In `convert-to-openai-responses-input.ts`: When `reasoningId` is null but `reasoningEncryptedContent` is present, still include the reasoning item (matching the vercel/ai#12869 fix)
3. In `transform.ts`: Ensure `include: ["reasoning.encrypted_content"]` is always set for OpenAI reasoning models, not only in variant options

